<div class="page-head"><div><a class="back-link" href="/accounting#customer-<%= invoice.id %>">‹ Customer balance</a><p class="eyebrow">Customer refund</p><h1>Record a refund for <%= invoice.invoice_number %></h1><p class="lede">Refund money and returned inventory are separate facts. This screen records only the financial refund; it will never add stock.</p></div></div>

<div class="notice"><div><strong><%= invoice.customer_name %> · Original sale <%= helpers.money(invoice.total_minor,invoice.currency) %></strong><br>Customer balance still open: <%= helpers.money(invoice.balance_minor,invoice.currency) %>. If merchandise physically came back, record that return through the inventory/Sales return evidence too.</div></div>

<form method="post" action="/accounting/refunds" class="stack-xl"><input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>"><input type="hidden" name="invoiceId" value="<%= invoice.id %>"><input type="hidden" name="originalJournalEntryId" value="<%= originalJournalEntryId %>">
  <section class="card"><div class="card-head"><h2>What actually happened?</h2></div><div class="card-body grid grid--2"><label class="field"><span class="field-label">Refund amount</span><input class="input" name="amount" inputmode="decimal" required placeholder="0.00"></label><label class="field"><span class="field-label">Refund date</span><input class="input" type="date" name="refundDate" value="<%= today %>" required></label><label class="field"><span class="field-label">Where should the refund reduce?</span><select class="select" name="refundFrom"><option value="unpaid">Reduce money the customer still owes</option><option value="cash">Cash was returned to the customer</option></select></label><label class="field"><span class="field-label">Reference / reason</span><input class="input" name="reference" maxlength="120"></label></div></section>
  <div class="form-actions"><button class="btn btn--primary" type="submit">Record refund</button><span class="hint">The original sale remains in history. Foundry records the refund as a separate, traceable event.</span></div>
</form>
